  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving access to life-saving quality and confidential GBV services to women and girls in drought-impacted locations of Kahda, Daynile, Baidoa, Galkacyo, Beletweyne and Kismayo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $1.5 million UNFPA project is to provide vulnerable people, especially women and girls, with access to confidential, safe and timely services and support items specialized on gender-based violence. To that end, UNFPA will distribute dignity kits to 13,255 people, provide case management, psychosocial support and specialized medical services for more than 5,000 people and provide $30,000 in cash assistance to 600 highly vulnerable people, among other life-saving activities. In total, UNPFA will reach 22,461 people, including 4,561 women, 5,770 children and 5,200 people living with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
